WEBVTT

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:16.100
Yes?

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:20.200
<i>Hello, Teshigawara-sensei?
It's Uchiyamada.</i>

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.010
<i>What's happened?</i>

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:24.550
<i>The special advanced class
is about to begin!</i>

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:26.400
I'm sorry.

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:30.130
I'm not feeling too well...

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.360
Could you please let me
rest for a while?

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:34.500
<i>For a while?</i>

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.300
That presents us with a problem,
Teshigawara-sensei!

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.610
<i>Without you, what will happen
to the special advanced class?</i>

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.220
What are we going to do, sir?

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:53.200
They say when the elite
are set back,

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.000
it takes time for them to recover.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.800
The special class is our creation.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:00.200
If it fails, what will
the parents say!

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:01.750
I know already!

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:04.010
- Fuyutsuki-sensei.
- Yes?

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:08.850
For now, could you switch
English for the first hour?

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:09.850
But...

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:13.420
Could you hurry, and explain
to the students too.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:14.780
I understand.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.700
That takes care of the first hour,

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:21.600
but what will do about
Mathematics?

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.240
We can't cancel Mathematics.

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:29.030
There is no choice, I'll do it!

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:32.100
Will you be okay?

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:35.200
I must keep it going.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.700
It's important to keep in contact
with the students.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:41.040
It's important for face
to face contact.

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:43.280
Magnificent!

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:46.100
And in the future, when you
become principal,

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:48.200
you won't have the opportunity
to do that.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:50.010
I'm not saying this
because of that!

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:51.500
I've felt that it was strange

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:53.400
to leave the principal's
post open.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:56.400
The head teacher is expected
to become the next principal.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.200
Just what is the director thinking!

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.280
Sir,

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:03.600
when that time comes,
you'll become the head teacher.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.470
Oh no! I'm not...

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.820
Please, Principal.

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:15.210
Thank you, Head Teacher!

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:20.660
Onizuka! You again!

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:22.900
Wake up! What are you doing!

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:26.200
- Oh, good morning.
- Didn't we tell you!

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.620
Don't ever use this
as a hotel room!

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.110
I wasn't!

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:32.700
I'm the security guard,
so I have to make rounds.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.600
That being the case,
I figured it best

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:37.400
to be in the most valuable spot,
the principal's office.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:38.700
Onizuka-sensei!

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.360
- I got the watermelon!
- Thanks!

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:43.120
I thought we could eat
it together...

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:44.790
Fujitomi-sensei,

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.340
what are you doing here too!

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:47.490
Yes, well...

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:49.860
I invited him. I asked him
to come to school.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.500
Excuse me, but there's nothing
for me to do at home.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.390
No matter how much A/C
there's in this room,

00:02:56.390 --> 00:03:00.670
it isn't a place for you
to relax and rest!

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:03.190
If you keep doing this,
I won't forgive you!

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:05.840
- Get out!
- What a grump.

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:11.490
Shaddap!

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:15.970
Oh, geeze!

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:17.750
Man it's hot!

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:20.290
This ain't fun either.

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:26.740
Oh, Onizuka-sensei! How about it,
why don't you join us?

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:31.120
I'll pass, I don't need
the exercise.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:35.570
Come on! When it's hot,
it's best to sweat it out!

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:37.400
If you stay in where there's A/C,

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:40.200
you'll end up sick like
Teshigawara-sensei.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.200
I know already!

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.500
You know, I've always thought
that something

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.300
was wrong with
Teshigawara-sensei,

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.800
with his obsession with
university admissions.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:50.300
The most important thing
is that the student

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.200
and teachers share their feelings.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:53.800
Don't you think that's the key?

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:56.900
Not that I'm boasting,
but I've never

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:58.950
resorted to corporal punishment.

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:00.700
If you appeal to their hearts,

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:03.900
then the students will
understand your feelings.

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:07.550
In reality, there are no bad kids.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.010
That is how I truly feel.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:12.400
Could it be...

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:15.000
Hakamada-sensei, did you idolize
Kinpachi-sensei

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.600
and decided to become
a teacher because of that?

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:20.100
- You can tell?
- Hey, I'm "Super"!

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:24.090
I've seen that about
a hundred times!

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:28.400
"I am not teaching rotten apples!"

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.400
"They're living human beings!"

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:33.000
I like Nakamura Masatoshi too.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.400
"Tears are the sweat of the soul!"

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:38.370
- I know, Onizuka-sensei.
- Huh?

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:40.640
Your worried about your class,
2-4, aren't you?

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:41.700
Terrible, isn't it?

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:44.300
Saying they're boycotting class
until they get

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:47.300
- a different homeroom teacher.
- That's right! They're so brazen!

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:48.800
Alright then, I'll help you out!

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:49.800
What?

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:52.800
In any case, it's hot, so could you
stand at least a meter away?

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:55.300
I will convince everyone
to return to your class.

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:57.300
If you don't by fall,
you'll be fired, right?

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.500
Yeah, but I'm sure something'll
happen by then...

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:01.900
You know, I'm pretty popular
with the students.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:04.600
I don't know how many
chocolates I got on Valentines!

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:06.890
- Hakamada-sensei...
- Leave it to me!

00:05:06.890 --> 00:05:09.300
If I convince Murai Kunio
and Aizawa Miyabi,

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:10.800
then something will happen.

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:13.680
- They control the class.
- Yes, but I...

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:17.100
Don't worry about it!

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:20.810
Leave it to me!
I will find a solution!

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:25.890
Oh, geeze...

